944 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (With visibility established, the second phase tests assumptions. The industry data is unambiguous about why. More than 60% of organizations believe they can recover from downtime within hours; 35% actually can. Only 28% of ransomware victims fully restore their data. The only way to know which category an organization falls into is to test. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
945 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (Execute a full restore from backup, not a file recovery but a system-level restore simulating an actual outage or ransomware scenario. Document time to recovery, data completeness, what failed, and what worked. Given that backup repositories are targeted in roughly nine of ten ransomware attacks, this is also the moment to evaluate whether current backups would survive an attack at all. That is the immutability question, and only about a third of organizations industry-wide can answer yes to it.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
