/Title (Fifty-nine percent of verified incidents began in the identity layer, not on devices, the same pattern Sophos found industry-wide. The managed client base's 63% MFA adoption is roughly 1.7 times the published SMB rate, and this quarter's incident distribution shows the exposure that remains. The 37% of users without MFA, and the covered users whose VPNs and legacy applications sit outside it, are the surface the identity-led incident pattern points at. MFA coverage, not MFA adoption, is becoming the metric that matters, and it is a natural candidate for future instrumentation in this index.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4498 0 R
/Prev 4559 0 R
/Next 4560 0 R
>>
endobj
